On Thu, 6 Oct 2005, Wolfram wrote:

> I've noticed lately that people are often talking about the merits of
> having a large stack of highly enchanted daggers for missile weapons.
> The main point seems to be that you don't have to wield them to fire
> them.
>
> But I have a question.  How many daggers are we talking about?  10...
> 50... a thousand?  And how do you go about enchanting 50 daggers to +5
> or higher?  Don't you need _alot_ of blessed enchant weapon scrolls?
> And do you enchant normal daggers, or wait with enchanting until you
> have enough elven daggers?
>
> In my games, as a Valkyrie, I usually collect about 5 good daggers and
> use them on neighbours, nymphs and other annoyances.  For normal
> critters I use my main weapon and I never use ?oEW on anything but
> artifacts.  But having a huge stack of high-damage daggers intrigues
> me, so if someone could post a short dagger stack tutorial it would be
> much appreciated.

As said, wield all of them, enchant all at once. Concerning weight,
daggers weight 10 each, max capacity (with maxed out STR and CON) is 1000.
Playing a bit of slash'em with the showweight option on is rather
illuminating on these issues.

Moreover daggers don't disappear when thrown (darts and arrow and bolts
do).

The trick is also to have all your multiple daggers identified and trying
to play with the buc status of the scrolls in order to minimize the number
of scroll to use (and re-stack daggers together asap).

Usually you don't need that many daggers since few monsters can survive
after, say, 5 +7 daggers (2 rounds of throwing...) Carrying between 5 and
10 seems to be sufficient in the early game. In the middle to late game,
you can switch to a bit more, maybe 15 or 20. Also notice that you won't
kill everything with daggers (if from a fighter class), only the things
you don't want to melee (c, h, ...) No need to 'waste' daggers on a Gnome
when Mojo can do the job, especially when there are many more dangerous
monsters waiting to suck your brain.

